# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Both the memory and time cost for Pauli propagation routines generally scale with the size to which the evolved operator is allowed to grow.\n"
msgstr "Pauli伝播ルーチンのメモリコストと時間コストはどちらも、一般に、発展する演算子の成長を許容するサイズに応じてスケールします。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`propagate_through_rotation_gates()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/pauli-prop/propagation#pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_rotation_gates \"pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_rotation_gates\"): As the Pauli operator is propagated in the Pauli basis under the action of a sequence of $N$ Pauli rotation gates of an $M$-qubit circuit, the number of terms will grow as $\\mathcal{O}(2^N)$ towards a maximum of $4^M$ unique Pauli components. To control memory usage, the operator is truncated after application of each gate, which introduces some error proportional to the magnitudes of the truncated terms’ coefficients. The memory requirements are linear in the size of the evolved operator, and runtime scales linearly in both the operator size and the number of gates.\n"
msgstr "[`propagate_through_rotation_gates()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/pauli-prop/propagation#pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_rotation_gates \"pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_rotation_gates\"): $M$量子ビット回路の$N$個のPauli回転ゲートの列の作用の下でPauli演算子がPauli基底で伝播されると、項数は$\\mathcal{O}(2^N)$で増加し、最大$4^M$個の固有のPauli成分に向かいます。メモリ使用量を抑えるために、各ゲートの適用後に演算子が切り捨てられ、切り捨てられた項の係数の大きさに比例する誤差が生じます。メモリ要件は発展した演算子のサイズに対して線形であり、実行時間は演算子のサイズとゲート数の両方に対して線形にスケールします。\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "[`propagate_through_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/pauli-prop/propagation#pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_operator \"pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_operator\"): Conjugates one operator in the Pauli basis by another by greedily accumulating terms in the sum, $\\sum_{i,j,k}G^{\\dagger}_iO_jG_k$, where $i,j,k$ are sparse indices over the Pauli basis. This implementation sorts the coefficients in each operator by descending magnitude then searches the 3D index space for the terms with the largest coefficients, starting with the origin $(0,0,0)$, and accumulating $(i,j,k)$ triplets up to a specified cutoff. The time spent searching can often be made negligible by increasing the search step size in $(i,j,k)$ space, which provides a cubic speedup for this subroutine. In our profiling, significant time can be spent sorting the operators and performing Pauli multiplication to generate the terms in the new operator.\n"
msgstr "[`propagate_through_operator()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/pauli-prop/propagation#pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_operator \"pauli_prop.propagation.propagate_through_operator\"): 和$\\sum_{i,j,k}G^{\\dagger}_iO_jG_k$の項を貪欲に累積することで、Pauli基底のある演算子を別の演算子で共役変換します。ここで$i,j,k$はPauli基底上のスパースな指標です。この実装では、各演算子の係数を大きさの降順に並べ替え、原点$(0,0,0)$から始めて、係数が最大の項を3次元の指標空間で探索し、指定されたカットオフまで$(i,j,k)$の3つ組を累積します。$(i,j,k)$空間での探索のステップサイズを大きくすることで、探索に費やす時間はしばしば無視できる程度にでき、このサブルーチンでは3乗の高速化が得られます。私たちのプロファイリングでは、演算子の並べ替えや、新しい演算子の項を生成するためのPauli乗算に、かなりの時間が費やされることがあります。\n"

